# The repo root sets `* text=auto eol=lf`, which is right for everything that is
# source and catastrophic for everything here. These payloads are raw IEEE-754
# and raw bytes: git's text heuristic only looks for a NUL in the first 8 kB, and
# `tree_identity/predictions.f32` genuinely has none — so a `0x0D 0x0A` pair
# occurring inside a float would be "normalized" to `0x0A` on checkout, silently
# shortening the matrix and rewriting the very numbers the gate compares. The
# gate would then fail on a machine whose only sin was checking the repo out.
*.f32   binary
*.i8    binary
*.onnx  binary
*.json  text eol=lf
